course: dictionary
lesson: 12695
title: Divinity: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which are its context. «Christians believe in the divinity of Jesus.» Here divinity means being God, because the sentence is about belief in God.
explain: Divinity can also mean a god or goddess. «The Romans prayed to many divinities.» The clue is many: there were lots of gods and goddesses, so divinities means gods and goddesses.
explain: Divinity can mean the study of religion and God. You may see it in «a divinity school», where people learn to become church leaders. Think about the sentence first, then choose the meaning that fits.
fact: Divinity is a noun. Its plural is divinities.
fact: «Divinity» means the quality of being God or a god, or being divine.
fact: «Divinities» means gods or goddesses, such as Zeus and Jupiter in old Greek and Roman stories.
fact: «Divinity» can also mean the study of religion and God, which is also called theology.
fact: In America, «divinity» can mean a soft white sweet made with egg whites and sugar.
exercise: «Christians believe in the divinity of Jesus.» What does divinity mean here? | A school subject about numbers | A large church building | A soft white sweet | *Being God
exercise: «The ancient Greeks worshipped many divinities, such as Zeus.» What does divinities mean? | Holy books | *Gods and goddesses | Old stone walls | Clever teachers
exercise: Which sentence uses divinity to mean a soft white sweet? | «The Romans built a temple to their divinities.» | «She studied divinity at university.» | *«She bought a bag of soft white divinity from the shop.» | «Divinity is about being divine.»
test: «She is studying divinity at university, learning about God and religion.» What does divinity mean here? | Being very clever | *The study of religion and God | A soft white sweet | A god with wings
test: «The old story tells of a goddess, a divinity who lived on the mountain.» What does divinity mean here? | A school for teachers | *A god or goddess | A kind of mountain | A holy building
exam: Which meaning fits «the divinity of Christ»? | A school for teachers | A soft sweet | A type of bird | *Being God or divine
